why: ran because operand 3 is a command-substitution `$(...)` or runtime-dynamic value -- its value couldn't be resolved (first seen at 2:17 `apt-get install -y "$1"`); so dorc runs it, to stay safe (when unsure, run). to skip it, make the operand a literal Dorc can resolve+probe [resolve-dynamism]
